WEBVTT

00:00.400 --> 00:03.150
- [Instructor] The base of a
solid is the region enclosed

00:03.150 --> 00:06.190
by the graphs of y is
equal to negative x squared

00:06.190 --> 00:10.350
plus six x minus one
and y is equal to four.

00:10.350 --> 00:15.010
Cross sections of the solid
perpendicular to the x-axis

00:15.010 --> 00:18.320
are rectangles whose height is x.

00:18.320 --> 00:22.530
Express the volume of the
solid with a definite integral.

00:22.530 --> 00:25.790
So pause this video, and see
if you can have a go at that.

00:25.790 --> 00:27.210
All right, now what's
interesting about this

00:27.210 --> 00:29.260
is they've just given us the
equations for the graphs,

00:29.260 --> 00:31.140
but we haven't visualized them yet.

00:31.140 --> 00:32.970
And we need to visualize
them, or at least I like

00:32.970 --> 00:35.480
to visualize them so I can
think about this region

00:35.480 --> 00:36.930
that they're talking about.

00:36.930 --> 00:39.210
So maybe a first thing
to do is think about,

00:39.210 --> 00:42.200
well, where do these two lines intersect?

00:42.200 --> 00:44.320
So when do we have the same y-value?

00:44.320 --> 00:45.420
Or another way to think about it is

00:45.420 --> 00:48.070
when does this thing equal four?

00:48.070 --> 00:49.680
So if we set them equal to each other,

00:49.680 --> 00:51.750
we have negative x squared

00:51.750 --> 00:55.240
plus six x minus one is equal to four.

00:55.240 --> 00:56.600
This will give us the x-values

00:56.600 --> 00:58.160
where these two lines intersect.

00:58.160 --> 01:02.740
And so we will get, if
we want to solve for x,

01:02.740 --> 01:04.980
we can subtract four from both sides.

01:04.980 --> 01:09.980
Negative x squared plus six x
minus five is equal to zero.

01:10.720 --> 01:13.110
We can multiply both
sides by negative one.

01:13.110 --> 01:16.200
We will get x squared minus six x

01:16.200 --> 01:18.660
plus five is equal to zero.

01:18.660 --> 01:21.460
And then this is pretty
straightforward to factor.

01:21.460 --> 01:23.310
One times five is five,

01:23.310 --> 01:26.360
or actually I say negative one
times negative five is five.

01:26.360 --> 01:29.690
And negative one plus
negative five is negative six.

01:29.690 --> 01:32.090
So it's going to be x minus one

01:32.090 --> 01:35.280
times x minus five is equal to zero.

01:35.280 --> 01:39.140
And so these intersect
when x is equal to one

01:39.140 --> 01:41.890
or x is equal to five.

01:41.890 --> 01:43.720
Since we have a negative out front

01:43.720 --> 01:45.590
of the second-degree term right over here,

01:45.590 --> 01:49.070
we know it's going to be a
downward-opening parabola.

01:49.070 --> 01:52.750
And we know that we
intersect y equals four

01:52.750 --> 01:55.220
when x is equal to one and x equals five.

01:55.220 --> 01:58.130
And so the vertex must
be right in between them,

01:58.130 --> 02:00.630
so the vertex is going
to be at x equals three.

02:00.630 --> 02:03.350
So let's actually visualize
this a little bit.

02:03.350 --> 02:05.980
So it's going to look something like this.

02:05.980 --> 02:07.650
I'll draw it with some perspective
'cause we're gonna have

02:07.650 --> 02:10.120
to think about a three-dimensional shape.

02:10.120 --> 02:13.220
So that's our y-axis.

02:13.220 --> 02:14.680
This is

02:15.720 --> 02:17.450
our

02:17.450 --> 02:19.120
x-axis.

02:19.120 --> 02:21.020
And let me draw some y-values.

02:21.020 --> 02:22.340
So one,

02:22.340 --> 02:23.470
two,

02:23.470 --> 02:24.600
three,

02:24.600 --> 02:26.120
four,

02:26.120 --> 02:27.400
five,

02:27.400 --> 02:28.420
six,

02:28.420 --> 02:30.300
seven, eight.

02:30.300 --> 02:31.960
This is probably sufficient.

02:31.960 --> 02:33.930
Now we have y is equal to four,

02:33.930 --> 02:36.370
which is going to look
something like this.

02:36.370 --> 02:38.310
So that is

02:38.310 --> 02:39.883
y is equal to four.

02:41.220 --> 02:44.060
And then we have y is
equal to negative x squared

02:44.060 --> 02:47.130
plus six x minus one,
which we know intersects

02:47.130 --> 02:49.650
y equals four at x equals
one or x equals five.

02:49.650 --> 02:51.670
So let's see, one,

02:51.670 --> 02:52.750
two,

02:52.750 --> 02:53.990
three,

02:53.990 --> 02:54.960
four,

02:54.960 --> 02:55.820
five.

02:55.820 --> 02:59.370
So x equals one, so we have
that point right over there.

02:59.370 --> 03:01.890
One comma four, and then
we have five comma four.

03:01.890 --> 03:05.770
And then we know the vertex
is when x is equal to three,

03:05.770 --> 03:07.100
so it might look something like this.

03:07.100 --> 03:08.840
We could substitute three back in here.

03:08.840 --> 03:13.170
So let's see, y will
equal to negative nine,

03:13.170 --> 03:14.310
three squared,

03:14.310 --> 03:16.140
plus 18

03:16.140 --> 03:17.420
minus one.

03:17.420 --> 03:18.580
And so what is that going to be?

03:18.580 --> 03:20.750
That's going to be y is
going to be equal to eight.

03:20.750 --> 03:23.060
So we have the point three comma eight.

03:23.060 --> 03:26.120
So this is five, six, seven,
eight, yep, right about there.

03:26.120 --> 03:29.200
And so we are dealing with a situation,

03:29.200 --> 03:31.390
we're dealing with a situation that looks

03:31.390 --> 03:33.650
something like this.

03:33.650 --> 03:36.750
This is the region in question.

03:36.750 --> 03:38.940
So that's going to be
the base of our solid.

03:38.940 --> 03:40.960
And they say cross sections of the solid

03:40.960 --> 03:43.120
perpendicular to the x-axis,

03:43.120 --> 03:44.770
so let me draw one of
those cross sections.

03:44.770 --> 03:49.390
So this is a cross section
perpendicular to the x-axis,

03:49.390 --> 03:52.540
are rectangles, whose height is x,

03:52.540 --> 03:55.423
so this is going to have
height x right over here,

03:56.270 --> 03:57.410
height x.

03:57.410 --> 04:01.200
Now what is this, the
width, I guess we could say,

04:01.200 --> 04:02.920
of this rectangle?

04:02.920 --> 04:03.890
Well, it's going to be the difference

04:03.890 --> 04:05.180
between these two functions.

04:05.180 --> 04:06.090
It's going to be these,

04:06.090 --> 04:09.110
this upper function minus
this lower function.

04:09.110 --> 04:11.930
So it's going to be, that
right over there is going

04:11.930 --> 04:16.920
to be negative x squared
plus six x minus one

04:16.920 --> 04:19.680
and then minus four,

04:19.680 --> 04:21.420
minus the lower function.

04:21.420 --> 04:24.700
So that could be simplified
as negative x squared

04:24.700 --> 04:27.400
plus six x minus five.

04:27.400 --> 04:29.390
And so if we wanna figure out the volume

04:29.390 --> 04:32.140
of this little section right over here,

04:32.140 --> 04:35.740
we'd multiply x times this,

04:35.740 --> 04:37.270
and then we would multiply that

04:37.270 --> 04:39.400
times an infinitesimal small,

04:39.400 --> 04:42.780
infinitesimally small depth, dx.

04:42.780 --> 04:47.030
And then we can just
integrate from x equals one

04:47.030 --> 04:48.580
to x equals five.

04:48.580 --> 04:49.500
So let's do that.

04:49.500 --> 04:52.060
The volume of just this
little slice over here

04:52.060 --> 04:53.350
is going to be the base,

04:53.350 --> 04:58.100
which is negative x squared
plus six x minus five,

04:58.100 --> 05:01.950
times the height, times x,

05:01.950 --> 05:05.020
times the depth, times dx.

05:05.020 --> 05:08.580
And then what we wanna do is
we wanna sum up all of these.

05:08.580 --> 05:10.480
So you could imagine right
over here, you would have,

05:10.480 --> 05:12.480
or like right over here,

05:12.480 --> 05:14.160
you would have a cross
section that looks like this.

05:14.160 --> 05:15.800
X is now much larger.

05:15.800 --> 05:19.450
The height is x, so now it
looks something like this.

05:19.450 --> 05:21.120
So I'm just drawing two cross sections,

05:21.120 --> 05:23.320
just so you get the idea.

05:23.320 --> 05:24.350
So these are the,

05:24.350 --> 05:26.950
this is any one cross
section for a given x,

05:26.950 --> 05:28.350
but now we want to integrate.

05:28.350 --> 05:32.490
Our x is going from x
equals one to x equals five,

05:32.490 --> 05:35.450
x equals one to x equals five.

05:35.450 --> 05:37.700
And there you have it, we
have expressed the volume

05:37.700 --> 05:40.440
of that solid as a definite integral.

05:40.440 --> 05:41.740
And it's worth noting that this is,

05:41.740 --> 05:44.640
that this definite integral,
if you distribute this x,

05:44.640 --> 05:46.840
if you multiply it by all of these terms,

05:46.840 --> 05:47.810
it's very solvable.

05:47.810 --> 05:48.643
You don't need a,

05:48.643 --> 05:50.120
or it's very solvable
without a calculator.

05:50.120 --> 05:51.970
You're just going to get
a polynomial over here

05:51.970 --> 05:53.810
that you have to take
the antiderivative of

05:53.810 --> 05:56.083
in order to evaluate
the definite integral.
